  "title": "The Game Chromatic Number of the Thirteen-Vertex Graph M3(C3)",
  "batch_label": "50",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let H=M_3(C_3) be the 13-vertex graph defined in problem.md, and play the standard proper vertex-coloring game with Alice moving first and a common set of four colors. Alice has a winning strategy from the empty position. Moreover H is not three-colorable by the forced-layer argument in evidence/research.md; consequently the game chromatic number is chi_g(M_3(C_3))=4. This statement is only for the layer parameter k=3.",
